zig (0.17.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release, based on upstream's amd64 and arm64 binaries:

    <https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/zig-x86_64-linux-0.17.0.tar.xz>
    <https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/zig-aarch64-linux-0.17.0.tar.xz>

  * Add debian/fetch-orig-source, which verifies the upstream SHA-256 and
    minisign signature before repacking the orig tarball.
  * Install to /usr/lib/zig without a version-specific path, so new upstream
    releases only need a changelog entry.
  * Refuse to build when the orig tarball's binary does not match the host
    architecture; smoke-test the compiler during the build.
  * Do not strip or dwz the upstream binary.
  * Switch to debhelper compat 13; Standards-Version 4.7.3;
    Rules-Requires-Root: no.
  * Point Vcs-* at the packaging repository, and upstream links at Codeberg.
  * Update the watch file to version 4 and upstream's index.json.
  * Refresh lintian overrides for current lintian and upstream layout.
  * Rewrite debian/copyright to cover the third-party code bundled in lib/
    and statically linked into the compiler.
  * New maintainer.

 -- Daniel Fox <danudey@me.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:06:16 -0700

